# Docker reads only the build context's own .dockerignore, and `contracts/` is supplied to
# the runner-service, control-plane, and github-integration builds as a separate named context
# (compose's `additional_contexts`). Without this file every family tool's local `node_modules`
# and any stray secret would be sent to the daemon — and, for github-integration, copied into
# the runtime image by `COPY --from=contracts . /app/contracts`. The sibling service contexts
# (agents/, control-plane/, apps/*/) exclude the same patterns; keep them in step.
**/node_modules
.env
*.pem
*.log

# Each family's `tools/` is a large build-only working tree (`pnpm install`ed, ~90 MB). The
# images copy the contract tree with `COPY --from=contracts integration-contract ...` and read
# only `schemas/` (Runner) or just the OpenAPI document (control-plane); `tools/` is never read
# at build or run time. Excluding it here keeps it out of the build context and the images
# without the Dockerfile needing the newer `COPY --exclude` flag.
**/tools
